    "final_answer": "Fog horns typically operate at low frequencies, usually between **250 Hz and 400 Hz** (roughly 1/3 to 1/2 octave below normal speech). This low frequency allows the sound to travel long distances through fog and other atmospheric conditions.\n\nThe most common standard frequency is around **300-350 Hz**, which provides an optimal balance between:\n- Long-distance propagation (low frequencies travel farther)\n- Audibility over background noise\n- Avoiding interference with ship communication frequencies\n\nSome modern electronic fog horns may use slightly different frequencies, but they generally stay within this low-frequency range for maximum effectiveness."
